# ScienceCode verifies artifacts by SHA-256 over exact bytes. Line-ending
# translation would change those bytes, so a record hashed on one machine would
# fail verification on another. Check out every text file exactly as committed.
* -text

# Formats that carry hashed or byte-exact content, marked binary so git never
# diffs or translates them.
*.png binary
*.stl binary
*.step binary
*.onnx binary
*.tgz binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
